From fcf7e4b5ea9c7b8f2e805953e17bd7a954bdb7aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artemonim <Artemonim@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 22:00:43 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/23] fix(agent): principal-review hardening for service
 tiers

- Preserve user-supplied request_overrides service_tier/speed on the wire:
  only framework-baked tier keys (tracked via _framework_baked_tier_keys)
  are re-resolved per request; raw overrides pass through when no framework
  tier source applies (restores main's delegation.request_overrides contract)
- Open auto/cold bounded windows after primary-runtime restoration so a
  restored primary's first request gets its window (deadline stays
  turn-start)
- Hard-block TTFT escalation for curator and background-review agents
  (background-task exclusion now matches the docs)
- Aux service_tier shortcut is OpenRouter-only on every aux slot (aux
  client, curator, background review); first-party routes omit the key
  with a one-time warning, matching the docs
- Remove dead gateway/TUI escalation loaders; replace frozen-default
  change-detector tests with contracts against DEFAULT_SERVICE_TIER_ESCALATION;
  soften the default-off overhead wording to match the implementation

Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>
